---
source: crates/rustman-cli/src/tests.rs
expression: help
---
Call a tool of an MCP server

Usage: rustman mcp-client call [OPTIONS] <SERVER> <TOOL>

Arguments:
  <SERVER>
          A server of the workspace, stdio:<command line> or an http(s):// URL

  <TOOL>
          The tool to call

Options:
      --json
          Print the result as JSON

      --trust
          Spawn a stdio server that is not trusted yet, and record the approval

      --timeout <DURATION>
          Give up on a request after this long (default: the server's timeout_ms, else 60s)

      --env <NAME>
          Environment (default: RUSTMAN_ENV, then default_environment)

      --workspace <DIR>
          Workspace directory (default: search from the current directory upwards)

      --args <JSON>
          The arguments as one JSON object

      --arg <K=V>
          One argument: k=v for a string, k:=JSON for any JSON value (repeatable)

      --no-validate
          Send arguments that break the tool's input schema anyway

      --sampling-response <FILE>
          Answer sampling requests with the CreateMessageResult in FILE (default: reject them)

      --color <WHEN>
          Color: auto (a terminal without NO_COLOR or TERM=dumb), always or never
          
          [default: auto]

  -v, --verbose...
          Log more on stderr: -v requests, -vv headers, -vvv everything (RUST_LOG, when set, replaces these levels)

  -h, --help
          Print help
